    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass, including the new `Cp22Tests`. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for `POST /api/owners`: when more than 80 owners have already been created for the request's registration business day, the created owner carries `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`. The flag is evaluated and fixed at creation, stored on the owner, and returned unchanged on later reads (matching how `getOwner` is used in the test).\n\nFollowing the existing OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, I:\n\n- **`AssignBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new pipeline function) \u2014 counts existing owners registered on the owner's resolved business day (the same per-day bucket `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` uses) and stamps `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80` onto the built owner in place, before it is saved (so it excludes itself).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in after `registrationDate` (so `registrationDate` is already business-day-adjusted) and before `customerCode`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` `Boolean` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n- **schema.sql** for all four DBs (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column; the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the hsqldb schema is authoritative.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `bulkSignupWarning` to the ignored targets on the request-DTO\u2192entity mapping, consistent with the other server-computed fields.\n\nFull suite: **33 tests, 0 failures**.",
